 - **Build inputs:** Mac libraries use `MACOS_MIN` from `dm/mac/min_os.mk`, matching the host's deployment target; otherwise a newer SDK emits libraries older supported Macs cannot load and the host falls back to runtime compilation. Every build rechecks the compiler, SDK, deployment target and source contents, reusing the header only when all match. Installing the Metal toolchain after a source-only build therefore regenerates the libraries without a clean build.
 - **Build callers:** the NSP packer and regression harness generate the Mac header before checking their cached host executables, and include it in the host fingerprint. The standalone iOS compile check generates the iPhone header before its dry run, as the app build does. A dry run alone does not generate either header.
+
+### Mesh primitive stores extend through the last block
+
+- **Symptom:** Ocarina's light-tile meshes can corrupt shared memory; upstream reports white blotches over Kokiri Forest from these meshes.
+- **Cause:** with primitive count zero, the guest's unsigned `count - 1` wraps and every lane in the final block writes index bytes. A maximum of 126 primitives still permits lanes 126 and 127 to store, past an array sized for only 126.
+- **Fix:** `dmsh_meshstage.memory` reserves complete blocks of 32 primitives for index storage (upstream PR #1575). The primitive reservation does not follow the vertex count. This changes the shader chain and needs rebuilt libraries.
+- **Check:** `test_dmsh_meshstage.py` models the guest's last index store for aligned and partial blocks; four cases fail before the correction. Stage compilation for macOS and iOS also passes. On-device correction of the intermittent flashes remains a separate validation.
+- **Found on:** [The Legend of Zelda: Ocarina of Time](../../dm/games/0400486024DEC000/README.md): active light-tile task `a5288d0a6c4971fd`, mesh `e8c667282ba7bd9b`, fragment `ea1bf96b72e72476`.
+
+### LDSM reads rows other lanes stored
+
+- **Symptom:** warp-cooperative shared-memory reads can observe stale or overwritten values, corrupting network output used by movie enhancement and upscaling.
+- **Cause:** NVIDIA implicitly orders a warp's shared stores and collective LDSM reads. Metal needs subgroup synchronization to order another lane's store and this lane's load; the old Ampere emitter generated neither boundary.
+- **Fix:** `InstEmitAmpereTensor.ALdsm` brackets the collective loads with `SubgroupBarrier`, emitted as `simdgroup_barrier(mem_flags::mem_threadgroup)`. The second boundary prevents a later store from reusing a row before all lanes read it. This changes the translator and the shader chain.
+- **Check:** `Shared.test_ldsm_reads_between_subgroup_barriers` translates an STS/LDSM/STS sequence and checks both memory barriers around the generated reads. It fails with the old translator; all 15 shared-memory instruction tests pass with the rebuilt translator. A local diagnostic also executes the translated STS/LDSM/STS sequence on an Apple M4, observing both the collective result and the later shared-memory reuse: 16,777,216 checked values across 64 rounds, no mismatch. This does not establish iPhone rendering correctness; game rendering needs its own device comparison.
+- **Found on:** [The Legend of Zelda: Ocarina of Time](../../dm/games/0400486024DEC000/README.md), investigated against upstream's LDSM synchronization finding; the extent to which it explains the local one-frame white flashes remains open.
+
+### Masked temporaries become uninitialized MSL reads
+
+- **Symptom:** Metal warns that a temporary bool is read uninitialized, including in active foliage compute and mesh shaders. A conditional store followed by a logical guard can produce `bool b; if (a) b = value; result = b || !a;`. The result does not depend on b when a is false, but MSL still reads b first.
+- **Cause:** the SPIR-V function temporary may have an undefined value on the unstored path; lowering it to a C++/MSL uninitialized bool introduces target-language undefined behavior instead of choosing a boolean value. A compiler warning alone does not establish the cause of a visible artifact.
+- **Fix:** the shared spirv-cross arguments request `--force-zero-initialized-variables`. This selects zero for undefined temporaries at the language boundary, including generated phi locals, without game-specific shader substitutions. It changes the shader chain and requires complete libraries.
+- **Check:** `test_dmsh_initialized.py` translates a synthetic masked function temporary through the chain's actual cross arguments: Metal `-Werror=uninitialized` fails before and passes after. With `DMSH_TEST_GPU=1`, 65,536 results match the defined logical expression on Metal. A local syntax audit found seven affected shaders among 631 bound in the forest capture; all seven translate without these diagnostics with the option. The option also initializes private arrays, so device performance and visual output must be compared before adoption.
+- **Found on:** [The Legend of Zelda: Ocarina of Time](../../dm/games/0400486024DEC000/README.md): foliage compute `5a2e37058f21c8a5`, `58f47abfa0a84773`, foliage meshes including `6a1ceebb6cff56dd`, investigated after the user identified the first flashing plant. Whether this resolves the observed full-scene white flashes remains open until device testing.
